<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Quartz</RootNamespace>
    <Title>Quartz.NET Weasel Integration for SQLite</Title>
    <Description>Quartz.NET Weasel integration for SQLite - the ADO.NET job store's tables as a Weasel model, applied by db-apply, resources setup or at startup; $(Description)</Description>
    <PackageTags>$(PackageTags);weasel;jasperfx;critter-stack;schema;migrations;sqlite</PackageTags>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- Signed like every Quartz package; Weasel.Sqlite and the rest of the JasperFx stack are not (CS8002). -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS8002</NoWarn>
    <!--
      The claim, read the way Quartz.csproj's is: no IL3050, proven by a run rather than argued.

      What is proven: Quartz.Trimming.Canary references this package, is published by ILCompiler as a native
      executable on Windows, Linux and macOS on every pull request, and is run. Under a real host,
      UseWeaselForSqlite() creates the schema on an empty file database in StartingAsync - through
      Quartz.Weasel's registrar, startup service and system part, and Weasel.Sqlite's migrator - and a store
      on it validates the schema, schedules a job, fires it and reads it back. SQLite is the one Weasel
      dialect that needs no server, which is why it is the one that can say this.

      What a native publish reports against this package and Quartz.Weasel: nothing. Weasel.Core reports one
      IL2093 of its own (MultiCommandDataReader.GetFieldType does not repeat DbDataReader's return
      annotation), which is Weasel's to fix and build/Build.cs logs rather than fails on. The db-apply,
      db-assert, db-patch and resources commands are JasperFx's and are not run by the canary.
    -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
    <EnableTrimAnalyzer>true</EnableTrimAnalyzer>
    <EnableAotAnalyzer>true</EnableAotAnalyzer>
    <EnableSingleFileAnalyzer>true</EnableSingleFileAnalyzer>
    <!--
      Off for the reason Quartz.Weasel.csproj gives. Here it also keeps the driver floor Weasel's: pinned,
      Microsoft.Data.Sqlite would enter this nuspec at the version the tests use rather than the one
      Weasel.Sqlite declares.
    -->
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>false</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Quartz.Weasel\Quartz.Weasel.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.Sqlite" VersionOverride="10.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="Weasel.Sqlite" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
